From: Raimondas Lencevicius <59739769+raimondasl@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:36:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Add offline full-game tests with a stub model

Runs Swarm end to end without a model or ARC's API: arc-agi loads a
two-level toy game written for the test (not an ARC game) from a temporary
ENVIRONMENTS_DIR, and the model is a stub HTTP transport that returns
canned actions through the real google-genai Interactions or OpenAI chat
client, installed via the client.transport_retry transport. A socket guard
fails the test on any connection to a non-loopback address.

- OPERATION_MODE=offline, every Gemini 3.8 Flash high path profile: the
  game is won in six actions; the notes sentence, thought replay and the
  175k harness-summary compaction appear exactly where each profile puts
  them; run_meta records arc_environment kind local.
- A lost life forces a RESET, the buffered GAME_OVER frame reaches the
  next request, and play continues to a win.
- The per-level action budget (5x baseline) and the optional cost guard
  end the run with ACTION_BUDGET and COST_CAP.
- The OpenAI chat stub plays the same game.
- Online mode against a local arc-agi server (create_app on 127.0.0.1,
  ARC_BASE_URL, no ARC_API_KEY) plays the game through
  RemoteEnvironmentWrapper.

